 "method": "By RM (or branch): proposal quality, review queries, conditions met, promises delivered, and how their approved decisions performed afterwards, risk-adjusted. Risk adjustment: observed defaults in the four quarters after each approval against expected defaults (sum of the 12-month PD at the decision, scaled so the whole history's O/E is 1), O/E with a Poisson interval, so an RM who books weaker borrowers is judged against the risk taken. Composite score 0-100: the percentile rank of each measure across RMs with enough history (quality 25%, conditions met 20%, promises delivered 15%, fewer queries 10%, O/E 30%). Fewer than MIN_N approved decisions is flagged thin and left out of the ranking.",
 "data_note": "Decision history is a fictional seed published to Data Domains (domain governance, gov_* relations, ops/r13_seed_governance.py); outcomes (stage, DPD, default, rating drift) are the corporate book's own."
}